  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, poll due 16 January 1928; seven nominations were reduced to six by the withdrawal of George M. Carter, so the six were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1928, p. 7). Retiring members John Graham, Charles M. Legg, William M'Cullough, Thomas J. Patterson and David C. Thomson sought re-election; James H. Taylor did not. Francis Atkinson (teacher) was the new member. Returned unopposed."
